# E0300: a method called through its type takes a value of that type as its
# receiver. `ys.length` would read the ListVal's own member; through
# `(List String)` it names a List's, and a ListVal is no List.
main: function is {
    ys: ListVal i64
    ys.append 3
    n: (List String).length ys
    print "\{n}"
}
